\DOC DISCARD_OLDSTATE_TAC

\TYPE {DISCARD_OLDSTATE_TAC : string -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Deletes from the assumption list every hypothesis that mentions a state
variable other than the one named, leaving the conclusion untouched.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {s : string} names the state variable whose assumptions are to be
kept. Applied to a goal {A ?- t}, the tactic discards those assumptions whose
statement involves some state variable other than the named one — typically
register/flag/memory reads, event-trace equations, and other state-indexed
facts about earlier states, including facts about the named state whose
right-hand side still refers to another state. Retained, in their original
relative order, are assumptions mentioning no state variable at all (arithmetic
side conditions, non-overlapping hypotheses, pure implications), those about
the named state only, and the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} assumption. Possibly
nothing is discarded.
{
          A ?- t
     ================  DISCARD_OLDSTATE_TAC s
          A' ?- t
}
\noindent where {A'} is {A} minus the discarded state-dependent assumptions.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of outcome, always on goals of
the same shape: an {eventually}-style conclusion about one state together with
a mixture of state-indexed and state-free assumptions.

\ENDDOC
